  "answer": "I'll look through the Shopizer checkout for how special prices with dates are applied on the storefront API.The end date is stored on the start-date field, and the price check then compares the start date to itself. I'll correct both.Creating a product through the admin API stored the special-price end date in the start-date field (`PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper`), so the storefront never saw an end date. The price calculation in `ProductPriceUtils` also compared the start date against itself when both dates were present, so a dated special was never applied. Both now use the end date, and specials with no dates are unchanged.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"storefront API response for a product whose special price has an end date\"], \"missing\": [\"a unit test or fixture that creates a product special with only an end date and with both dates, then reads the storefront price\"]}",
